    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1590">

                <pb facs="1007" n="891" xml:id="pg891"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.62/94.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Bevan to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-02T21:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 2, 1914, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>This afternoon German consular representative requested assistance of Admiral
                    Mayo and of this office to prevent local authorities from boarding the steamship
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Antonina</hi> of Hamburg-American line in transit
                    Europe and taking off Mexican accused of homicide. Captain believes that
                    accusation is mere pretext and man is wanted on political charges and refused
                    authorities permission to board ship. Authorities have placed a guard of
                    soldiers on the wharf with artillery and machine guns threaten to sink ship if
                    she attempts to leave the pier. This office has taken no action in the matter
                    and will not unless directed by Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bevan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
